    "Minimum Spanning Tree",
    "Prim's Algorithm",
    "Kruskal's Algorithm",
    "Borůvka's Algorithm"
  ],
  "statement": "You are given an array `points` representing integer coordinates of some points on a 2D-plane, where `points[i] = [x_(i), y_(i)]`.\n\nThe cost of connecting two points `[x_(i), y_(i)]` and `[x_(j), y_(j)]` is the **manhattan distance** between them: `|x_(i) - x_(j)| + |y_(i) - y_(j)|`, where `|val|` denotes the absolute value of `val`.\n\nReturn _the minimum cost to make all points connected._ All points are connected if there is **exactly one** simple path between any two points.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n![](./assets/min-cost-to-connect-all-points-1.png)\n```\nInput: points = [[0,0],[2,2],[3,10],[5,2],[7,0]]\nOutput: 20\nExplanation: \n\nWe can connect the points as shown above to get the minimum cost of 20.\nNotice that there is a unique path between every pair of points.\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: points = [[3,12],[-2,5],[-4,1]]\nOutput: 18\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n*   `1 <= points.length <= 1000`\n*   `-10^(6) <= x_(i), y_(i) <= 10^(6)`\n*   All pairs `(x_(i), y_(i))` are distinct.",
  "constraints": [
    "1 <= points.length <= 1000",
    "-106 <= xi, yi <= 106",
    "All pairs (xi, yi) are distinct."
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "input": "points = [[0,0],[2,2],[3,10],[5,2],[7,0]]",
